{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":776,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:laplacian-local-formula]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:smooth-local-extension]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","line":1144,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Laplacian is non-positive at an interior maximum]\n\\label{lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max}\n\n\\uses{lem:laplacian-local-formula}\n\n\n\n\nIf a smooth $v$ on an open $U\\subset M$ has a local maximum at $q$, then\n$dv(q)=0$ and $\\Delta v(q)\\le0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:smooth-local-extension,lem:differential-vanishes-at-max,lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max,lem:laplacian-local-formula}\nExtend $v$ smoothly near $q$. Its differential vanishes, and tracing the\nnegative semidefinite Hessian in an orthonormal basis gives\n$\\Delta v(q)\\le0$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Laplacian is non-positive at an interior maximum] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6c61706c616369616e2d6e6f6e706f7369746976652d61742d6d6178\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Alaplacian-local-formula\">↗ lem:laplacian-local-formula</a> <p></p>If a smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> on an open <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U\\subset M$\">$U\\subset M$</span> has a local maximum at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dv(q)=0$\">$dv(q)=0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta v(q)\\le 0$\">$\\Delta v(q)\\le 0$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Asmooth-local-extension\">↗ lem:smooth-local-extension</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Adifferential-vanishes-at-max\">↗ lem:differential-vanishes-at-max</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Ahessian-nonpositive-at-max\">↗ lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Alaplacian-local-formula\">↗ lem:laplacian-local-formula</a> Extend <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> smoothly near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>. Its differential vanishes, and tracing the negative semidefinite Hessian in an orthonormal basis gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta v(q)\\le 0$\">$\\Delta v(q)\\le 0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:smooth-local-extension","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hopf-strong-maximum","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:laplacian-local-formula","title":"lem:laplacian-local-formula","label":"lem:laplacian-local-formula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:smooth-local-extension","title":"lem:smooth-local-extension","label":"lem:smooth-local-extension"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","label":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","label":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hopf-strong-maximum","title":"lem:hopf-strong-maximum","label":"lem:hopf-strong-maximum"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Laplacian is non-positive at an interior maximum]\n\\label{lem:laplacian-nonpositive-at-max}\n\n\\uses{lem:laplacian-local-formula}\n\n\n\n\nIf a smooth $v$ on an open $U\\subset M$ has a local maximum at $q$, then\n$dv(q)=0$ and $\\Delta v(q)\\le0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:smooth-local-extension,lem:differential-vanishes-at-max,lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max,lem:laplacian-local-formula}\nExtend $v$ smoothly near $q$. Its differential vanishes, and tracing the\nnegative semidefinite Hessian in an orthonormal basis gives\n$\\Delta v(q)\\le0$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:laplacian-local-formula","title":"lem:laplacian-local-formula","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:smooth-local-extension","title":"lem:smooth-local-extension","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","title":"lem:differential-vanishes-at-max","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","title":"lem:hessian-nonpositive-at-max","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}